-- Rifts World Book 4: Africa - its creatures: 24 rows for `creatures` and
-- their printed attacks in `stat_attacks` (owner_kind 'creature').
--
--   the Horsemen's creations (printed 15-27): Nightmare Zombie, Devil Skull,
--     Magic Beetle
--   Minions of the Gods (printed 65-70): Jinn (`jinn-africa`; `jinn` is the
--     Palladium Fantasy row), and the Children of Amon's three bio-wizard
--     organisms - Transfortifier, Chest Amalgamate, Zombitron
--   Wildlife and Monsters (printed 127-131): Wildebeest, Cape Buffalo,
--     African Lion, Leopard, Typical Crocodile, Mokele-mbembe (the book's
--     "Erythrusuchus"), Massospondylus, Buti-fas, Demonic Cannibal
--   the NPC view of this book's eight playable races (playable = 1): Pygmy
--     Hunter, Pygmy Shaman, Agogwe, Tree People, Phoenixi (`phoenixi-africa`),
--     Ramen (`ramen-africa`), Tauton, Crocodillian. `phoenixi` and `ramen` are
--     Palladium Fantasy Dragons and Gods rows.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-africa-creatures.sql
--
-- ALL 24 ARE NEW: no slug existed in production on 2026-09-26.
--
-- EXTRACTED by four slices, every number read off a 150-200 dpi render rather
-- than the text layer, which mangles dice here (106 = 1D6, 304 = 3D4). Every
-- row passes creatureFormulaGaps (js/creature-roll.js), the grammar the "roll
-- creatures" endpoint uses; a pool or attribute the book does not print is
-- absent, and what a formula cannot hold is in pools_note.
--
-- ONLY PRINTED ATTACKS. Two slices first derived punch damage the book does not
-- print (the zombie's and devil skull's blows, the Ramen's and Tauton's punches
-- from the supernatural P.S. table); those were removed. The rows carry only
-- the damage the book states.
--
-- JUDGEMENT CALLS, each on its page: one Nightmare Zombie row with the giant
-- size in its notes (the encounter section restates the same block on printed
-- 157-158); one Jinn row, the four kinds differing only in element and spell
-- range; the Transfortifier's M.D.C. is the host's; the Erythrosuchus and
-- Massospondylus store the M.D.C. the book equates to their S.D.C.; the Demonic
-- Cannibal leaves out a sentence the book repeats by mistake from the Buti-fas.
-- The Agogwe's I.S.P. is the 60% minor tier, the others in pools_note.
--
-- description, natural abilities and notes are paraphrases, checked for any
-- eight-word run shared with the book's text (stat lines and name lists aside).

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'nightmare-zombie', 'Nightmare Zombie', 'undead', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"IQ":"6","ME":"N/A","MA":"N/A","PS":"24","PP":"20","PE":"20","PB":"6","Spd":"14"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4X100', NULL, NULL, 'M.D.C. 1D4X100 is for human- to horse-sized creations; giant ones (elephant-sized or larger) have 1D6X100. Physical attributes are supernatural. I.Q. is printed as roughly six with no imagination; the book says mental faculties are not really applicable, so M.E. and M.A. are not given. Giants add +10 P.S. (34) and +10 Spd (24). No alignment printed; they are mindless killers.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":2,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', 'Horror Factor 16 for giants. Giant, multi-limbed zombies are +6 to strike, parry and dodge instead of +4. One extra attack per melee for every two additional arms, tentacles or tail; extra heads and wings add nothing. Unaffected by drugs, gas, poison, possession or mind control, and know no fear.', NULL, 'Built by Death from stitched-together humanoid and animal remains, so no two look alike. Most winged ones fly at Spd 44 (about 30 mph). All physical attacks do M.D. Can follow simple orders but cannot decide, plan or disobey. Turn dead and protection circles repel or hold them off; silver, magic weapons and spells do double damage. One sent more than 100 miles from Death collapses after 60 days.', NULL, NULL, 'Human- to horse-sized; giant versions elephant-sized or bigger', NULL, 'Until destroyed; 60 days if more than 100 miles from Death', 'Anywhere Death travels in Africa; released ones roam freely', 'Death and the other Horsemen (never attacks them)', 'All living things', NULL, 'Patchwork animated corpses assembled by the Apocalypse demon Death from bones and body parts. Those under his control kill only those who attack them; those he releases hunt every living thing. The encounter section restates the same stat block on printed 157-158.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.15-16');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'devil-skull', 'Devil Skull', 'undead', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"IQ":"9","PS":"24","PP":"20","PE":"20","PB":"6","Spd":"22"}', NULL, NULL, '400', NULL, NULL, 'Physical attributes are supernatural. I.Q. printed as roughly nine. Spd 22 running, 58 flying (40 mph). M.E. and M.A. not printed.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":6,"parry":7,"dodge":7}', '+2 to save against magic and psionics. Impervious to mind control, poisons, drugs, gases, possession and normal fire. -1 with any mechanical weapon.', NULL, 'Winged flight. Smarter than zombies or animated dead: follows complex orders, decides rationally, cautious and cunning. Turn dead and simple protection circles do not affect them; superior circles and strong holy symbols hold them off. Spells, magic weapons and silver do double damage; Millennium Tree weapons do ten times damage.', NULL, NULL, '18 feet (5.5 m) tall', NULL, NULL, 'Carried as three horned skulls on the saddle of Death''s netherbeast', 'Death', NULL, NULL, 'Three horned skulls decorating Death''s saddle that he can turn into towering winged demonic skeleton warriors. They favour swords, clubs and especially magic weapons.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.18');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'magic-beetle', 'Magic Beetle', 'insect', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"154"}', NULL, NULL, '120', NULL, NULL, 'Only M.D.C., attacks, bonuses and flying speed are printed. Spd 154 is flying (105 mph). Six live in the hive of Pestilence''s Staff of Destruction; a destroyed beetle regrows in the hive after 24 hours.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":6}', NULL, NULL, 'Flight. Grows instantly to full size when released from the staff''s hive on command. Used to attack foes, kill livestock, ruin crops and steal.', NULL, NULL, '5 feet (1.5 m) long', NULL, 'Recreated 24 hours after destruction', 'The hive in Pestilence''s Staff of Destruction', 'Pestilence', NULL, NULL, 'Magical beetles kept in a tiny hive in the head of Pestilence''s rune staff, released to swell to five feet long and fly at his enemies.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.27');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'jinn-africa', 'Jinn, the Elemental Demon', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Any evil or selfish', '{"IQ":"1D6+8","ME":"2D6+10","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"1D6+14","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6X10"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6X100+200', '1D6X100', '1D4X10+30', 'Spd is running; flying speed is 2D6X10+100. By day all powers, attacks, bonuses and physical M.D.C. are halved. Growing above 16 ft adds 1D6 M.D.C. (the book does not say per foot; up to 24 ft).', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":4,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+4 dodge in flight, +6 pull punch, +4 roll with impact, +6 on all saving throws including horror factor; all in addition to attribute bonuses. Two attacks per melee if attacking by magic instead. Halve bonuses and attacks in daytime.', 'Basic math 98%, literate Dragonese/Elven 98% plus two languages of choice, streetwise 65%, intelligence 90%, track humans 50%, wilderness survival 70%, land navigation 85%, swim 80%, demon & monster lore 90%, faerie lore 90%, radio: basic 90%, computer operation 90%, basic electronics 90%, locksmith 80%, pick locks 90%, pick pockets 70%, palming 70%, concealment 70%, W.P. sword, W.P. energy rifle, plus three W.P. of choice.', 'Invisible by nature and can become visible or invisible at will; turns to mist at will; can metamorphose into an insect; fire and cold resistant (M.D. attacks do half); nightvision 90 ft (sees in total darkness); sees the invisible; dimensional teleport 53%; regenerates 3D6 M.D. each minute; understands every language by magic; can change size from 8 to 24 ft. The four kinds share these stats and differ only in element and spell range: black (earth, spell levels 1-8), white (water, 1-7), green (air, 1-7), yellow (fire, 1-8). Bound by the Curse of Thoth: whoever captures, defeats or rescues a jinn becomes its master and is owed three wishes, which the jinn fulfils by theft and trickery and twists where it can; Set can summon and command jinn. Vulnerable: creatures of twilight, at half strength in daytime; silver weapons do their S.D.C. damage as M.D.; Millennium Tree weapons, wands and staves do double damage.', 'Elemental (warlock) magic by kind: black jinn all earth spells levels 1-8, white all water 1-7, green all air 1-7, yellow all fire 1-8. Cast at 8th level proficiency, 4th during the day.', 'Rifts-style jinn: all sensitive and physical powers at 5th level proficiency (Palladium RPG-style jinn instead have all level one and two powers at 5th level).', '8 to 24 ft (2.4 to 7.3 m) tall; changes size at will', '1000 lbs (450 kg)', NULL, 'Native to an alien dimension; may turn up anywhere', 'Fellow demons of Hades; bound to Set by the Curse of Thoth', 'Humanoids generally and the forces of good', 'Not available as a player character; NPC or villain only.', 'A malicious, magic-wielding elemental demon of Hades that serves Set in Africa. Cursed to grant three wishes to any mortal who masters it, it grants them through theft and treachery.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.69-70');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'transfortifier', 'Transfortifiers', 'parasite', 'rifts', 0, 'Not applicable', '{}', NULL, NULL, '110', NULL, NULL, 'The microbe itself has no hit points (printed: not applicable). The M.D.C. is the infected host''s: its body becomes an M.D.C. structure starting at 110 and gaining 1D6X10 M.D.C. per level of experience or per ten years, whichever comes first. HP: none (printed as N/A or None).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Host gains +4 save vs poison, toxins, drugs and gases, +10% save vs coma/death, +1 save vs magic, +2 save vs horror factor.', 'Host''s skills are -10% from lost sensitivity of the skin.', 'Microbe that mutates a mortal host into a hulking M.D.C. being with thick rhino-like hide. Host is impervious to heat and cold, including magic cold, fire and plasma; P.S. becomes supernatural and gains 2 per level; grows six inches (0.15 m) per level or every 20 years. Side effects: +100 lbs (45 kg) per level or 10 years, P.B. -1 per level or ten years (to a floor of 3), Spd -2 per level; the host eventually cannot move and dies about 22 years after exposure. Only a purirobe (1-15% chance, retry every two days) or magic restoration (1-30%) within the first two months can remove it; after that it is permanent. Works on most animals, humans and D-Bees, not supernatural beings. Inhaled as a snuff or injected; reproduces continually. Amon''s second favorite organism.', NULL, NULL, 'Microscopic', NULL, '20+1D6 years inside a host; the host dies when they do', 'Inside a host: whole body, skin, organs and nervous system', NULL, NULL, 'Bio-wizard organism Amon inflicts on the Children of Amon; the row describes the organism and what it does to its host.', 'A bio-wizard microbe that turns its host into a thick-skinned, ever-growing mega-damage brute. The change keeps going until the host can no longer move and dies.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.65-66');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'chest-amalgamate', 'Chest Amalgamate (Chest Thing)', 'parasite', 'rifts', 0, 'Effectively anarchist', '{"IQ":"N/A"}', NULL, NULL, '4D4X10+20', NULL, NULL, 'I.Q. printed only as high animal intelligence. Once linked, the creature and its host share this one M.D.C. pool.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4}', 'Creature is +4 to save against magic, psionics and horror factor and impervious to poison and drugs. When threatened it can grant the host hyper-reactions: +1 initiative, +1 strike and dodge, double speed, one extra melee attack, +4 ft (1.2 m) leap. Host also +1 save vs magic and +10% save vs coma/death.', 'None; acts on instinct.', 'Crab-like symbiote that fuses into a humanoid host''s chest, sharing its lungs, blood and food; if either dies both die. Turns the host into a mega-damage being and can pump juicer-like chemicals into it: warns of danger and wakes the host, host never fatigues and needs four hours sleep, ignores injury penalties, heals twice as fast, is impervious to poisons, drugs, gases and disease, and lives 20 years longer. The creature stays active even if the host is incapacitated. Side effects: permanent deformity, +100 lbs (45 kg) and doubled appetite, and periodic cravings for blood and entrails from a fresh kill. Cannot be removed without killing the host. Tolerates other harmless parasites in the same host. Amon''s favorite organism.', NULL, NULL, 'Covers the whole chest, with tendrils running along neck and body', 'Adds 100 lbs (45 kg) to the host', '90 years', 'A humanoid or other intelligent host''s chest', NULL, NULL, 'Bio-wizard organism Amon inflicts on the Children of Amon.', 'A crab-like bio-wizard symbiote that grafts itself into a host''s chest, sharing its body and M.D.C. It fights with a retractable tentacle and a gaping chest mouth to keep its host alive.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.66');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'zombitron', 'Zombitron', 'parasite', 'rifts', 0, 'Effectively selfish in a mindless way', '{"Spd":"2D6"}', '2', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Spd 2D6 applies to both climbing and running.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '+4 to roll with impact or fall. Victim saves vs the trance on 15 or higher, -2 per zombitron beyond the first, rolled once per melee until entranced.', 'Climb 82%, prowl 50%, swim 40%.', 'Fuzzy tennis-ball-sized parasite on eight tiny black legs that clings to a host''s head, neck or spine and feeds on it. It puts the host in a zombie trance: the host obeys any command within its limits, has one melee action and no combat bonuses, and remembers nothing afterwards. A human host starves in 1D4 months unless fed; up to seven days does no lasting harm. The trance lasts until every zombitron is removed, which is easy with gloves, tongs or a stick. In the wild many may feed on one body and move on after it dies. Reproduces once a year, 1D6 live young. Mindless.', NULL, NULL, 'About the size of a tennis ball', NULL, 'Five years', 'Head, neck and spine of a host (most animals, humans and D-Bees)', NULL, NULL, 'Bio-wizard organism Amon uses on her most dangerous slaves (under 20% of her minions).', 'A tiny eight-legged bio-wizard parasite that drains its host while holding it in an obedient zombie trance. Amon reserves it for her most dangerous slaves.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.66-67');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'wildebeest', 'Wildebeest', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"22"}', '7D8', '1D4X10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Speed 22 is the average; it can burst to 44 (30 mph) for up to 1D6x10 minutes. The book prints no other attributes.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+3 S.D.C. damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '6 to 8 feet long (1.8 to 2.4 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Plains herds; grazes into forests and crosses rivers on migration.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Easily startled herd grazer; the big bulls charge, ram and stomp intruders, and 2D4 males may chase a fleeing party for a quarter mile.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.127');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'cape-buffalo', 'Cape Buffalo', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"22"}', '1D6X10', '1D6X10', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Speed 22 is the average; it can burst to 44 (30 mph) for up to 2D4x10 minutes. The book prints no other attributes.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+6 S.D.C. damage.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '6 to 8 feet long (1.8 to 2.4 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Plains herds; also grazes in forest meadows.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Aggressive herd animal that will not tolerate intruders; its bulls may even charge a vehicle, and a panicked herd of thousands flattens whatever lies ahead.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.127');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'african-lion', 'African Lion', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"18"}', '1D6X10', '40', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Speed 18 is the average; it can burst to 28 (19 mph) for 1D4 minutes. The book prints no other attributes.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"strike":3,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', '+6 S.D.C. damage.', 'Prowl 50%, climb 50%, swim 50%, track 70%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, '4 1/2 to 7 feet long (1.35 to 2.1 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Savanna tall grass near herds from the Serengeti and Ethiopia south, also forests; found as far north as Egypt.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The largest native cat, living in territorial prides where females do most hunting and males guard; a man-eater that has tasted humanoid flesh keeps hunting people.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.127-128');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'leopard', 'Leopard', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"22"}', '8D6', '30', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Speed 22 is the average; it can burst to 50 (35 mph) for 1D4 minutes. The book prints no other attributes.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":4}', '+3 S.D.C. damage.', 'Prowl 90%, climb 75%, track 50%.', 'Nightvision 60 feet (18.3 m); leaps 40 ft (12 m) across and 15 ft (4.6 m) straight up.', NULL, NULL, '4 1/2 to 6 feet long (1.35 to 1.8 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Trees of light to dense forest, often near water; sometimes prowls the plains.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Cunning tree-dwelling cat that ambushes from above and hauls its kill into the branches; about one in 40 is a black panther.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.128');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'typical-crocodile', 'Typical Crocodile', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"12"}', '6D6', '15', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'S.D.C. is 15 for small crocodiles and 30 for large ones; the formula stores the small value. Speed 12 is in water; 4 on land. The book prints no other attributes.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":2}', '+2 S.D.C. damage.', 'Swim 90%, prowl in water 75%.', 'Holds its breath underwater for 1D4+2 minutes; nightvision 60 feet (18.3 m). Seizes prey and drowns it.', NULL, NULL, '10 to 20 feet long (3 to 6 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Rivers and deep swamps across Africa; groups of 4D6, or 2D6x10 in large groups.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Large river reptile that eats mostly fish and small animals but will take antelope and humanoids, dragging them under to drown.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.128');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'mokele-mbembe', 'Erythrusuchus/Mokele-mbembe', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"33"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6X10', NULL, NULL, 'Printed as Hit Points/M.D.C.: 1D6x1000 S.D.C., stated as the equivalent of 1D6x10 M.D.C. Speed 33 in water, 20 on land. No other attributes printed.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":4,"dodge":3}', NULL, 'Swim 80%, prowl in water 80%.', 'Holds its breath underwater for 3D4 minutes; nightvision 60 feet (18.3 m).', NULL, NULL, '25 feet long (7.6 m) snout to tail tip', 'One ton', NULL, 'Larger, deeper rivers of the Congo and Zaire, also swamps and shallow rivers; fewer than 300 exist.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Grey, short-legged, long-tailed predator like a hippo crossed with a crocodile, the beast pygmies call Mokele-mbembe; it overturns canoes and bites victims in half. The book spells it Erythrusuchus; the real genus is Erythrosuchus.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.129');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'massospondylus', 'Massospondylus', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, NULL, '{"Spd":"18"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6', NULL, NULL, 'Printed as Hit Points/M.D.C.: 6D6x100 S.D.C., stated as the equivalent of 6D6 M.D.C. Speed 18; bursts to 44 (30 mph) for 2D4 minutes. No other attributes printed.', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":1,"dodge":6}', NULL, 'Swim 60%, prowl 55%.', 'Nightvision 60 feet (18.3 m). Usable as a riding animal, though dim and skittish.', NULL, NULL, '10 to 15 feet long (3 to 4.6 m) head to tail tip', NULL, NULL, 'Jungles of the Congo, Zaire, Angola and Zambia (about a thousand); travels in groups of 2D4.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Hippo-bodied, long-necked plant eater that also fits the Mokele-mbembe tales; probably an escaped transplant from another world, it shuns humanoids and predators.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.129');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'buti-fas', 'Buti-fas', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist or evil', '{"IQ":"9","ME":"10","MA":"6","PS":"18","PP":"14","PE":"17","PB":"4","Spd":"20"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+10', '2D4X10', '2D6X10+20', 'Attributes are printed as fixed averages. Supernatural creature.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+1 on all saving throws; bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. Attacks by hand to hand or psionics.', 'Basic math 90%, speaks Gobblely, Faerie and Swahili 98% plus 1D6 other languages, climb 80/75%, swim 80%, prowl 60%, track humans 75%, track animals 90%, land navigation 80%, wilderness survival 80%, horsemanship 90%.', 'Half damage from all magic; impervious to fire, heat and disease; nightvision 400 feet (122 m); heals twice as fast as humans; can take the shape of a white-headed owl whose eyes glow white.', 'None', 'Detect Psionics, Induce Sleep, Psychic Diagnosis, Psychic Surgery, See the Invisible, Mind Block, Empathy, Empathic Transmission, Psionic Empathy with Animals', '3 to 4 feet tall (0.9 to 1.2 m)', '75 lbs (34 kg)', '2000 years', 'Jungles and forests of the Congo, Zaire, Angola, Zambia, Nigeria and the Ivory Coast.', 'Panthers, monkeys and woodland animals; witches and evil spirits', 'Humans and human-looking D-bees', 'Roughly a 6th level scout. Uses no technology or cybernetics.', 'Small, foul-smelling forest spirits with white eyes, hair and beards who protect animals and torment humans from a distance; whether demon or faerie is unclear.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.129-130');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'demonic-cannibal', 'Demonic Cannibals', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant or diabolic', '{"IQ":"14","ME":"18","MA":"9","PS":"24","PP":"17","PE":"20","PB":"4","Spd":"33"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6+12', '2D6X10', NULL, 'Attributes are printed as fixed averages. P.B. 4 in demon form, 15 in human form. Spd 33 (22 mph) on foot, 50 flying as a vulture. Supernatural strength.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":5,"parry":7,"dodge":7}', '+2 to roll with impact, +2 to pull punch, paired weapons, +3 on all saving throws.', 'Basic math 80%, magically speaks all languages 98%, climb 70/65%, swim 50%, prowl 50%, track humans 75%, land navigation 75%, wilderness survival 90%, identify plants and fruits 75%, pilot sail, row and motor boats 75%, palming 75%, pick pockets 50%, W.P. knife, W.P. sword, one W.P. of choice.', 'Impervious to poison and disease; nightvision 200 feet (61 m); can shape change to look fully human; can turn into a vulture; supernatural strength; heals ten times faster than humans. Long knife-like thumbnail and a small toothed mouth on each finger.', 'None', 'None', 'Human size, 4 to 6 feet tall (1.2 to 1.8 m)', NULL, '1000 years', 'Jungles and forests, mainly the Congo, Ethiopia, Sudan and India.', 'Witches and other evil monsters; 1D4 stolen human children raised as their own', NULL, 'Roughly an 8th level warrior. About 40% wear M.D. body armor; little use for technology beyond weapons. Found alone, in groups of 3D4, or tribes of up to 4D6+12.', 'Human-seeming demons with pointed teeth who hunt and eat humanoids and scavenge fresh corpses, often passing as people with stolen children in tow.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.130-131');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'pygmy-hunter', 'Pygmy Hunter', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, mostly good or anarchist; very wary of large people, light-skinned humans and D-bees', '{"IQ":"3D6 min 10","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+2 min 12","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6+4"}', NULL, '30', NULL, '4D6', NULL, 'Attributes are human (all 3D6); the racial +2 P.E. and +4 Spd are folded in, and the I.Q./P.E. requirement of 10 is the floor before that bonus (so P.E. min 12). Hit points are not printed; as an ordinary human-scale race the usual P.E. +1D6 per level applies. S.D.C. 30 is the racial bonus; the Running skill adds +1D6 S.D.C., +1 P.E. and +4D4 Spd on top. P.P.E. +1D4 per level after the first. No psionics or I.S.P. printed.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":2}', '+1 on saves vs every kind of magic, +2 to save vs Horror Factor. Attacks per melee come from Hand to Hand: Expert (Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, for one other skill).', 'Native tongue and Euro (+20%); climb, prowl, running, track animals, land navigation and identify plants (+20% in the jungle, +10% elsewhere), wilderness survival, cook, preserve food, skin hides; W.P. Targeting, Blunt and one of choice; three related skills plus more at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12; two secondary.', 'High P.P.E. drawn from a spiritual bond with the jungle and the Millennium Tree. Pygmies who revere the Ancient Father cannot be forced by any means to reveal where it stands.', NULL, NULL, '4 to 5 ft (1.2 to 1.5 m)', NULL, NULL, 'The Congo jungles, in nomadic tribes of 3D4x10 to 2D6x100', 'Tree people; they revere the agogwe as sacred jungle spirits', 'Supernatural beings, seen as demons to be slain or driven off; suspicious of all foreigners', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C. The book notes that pygmy priests tend to be Millennium Druids and their medicine men Herbalists (Rifts England).', 'Small Congo jungle folk, among the best hunters and trackers in Africa, armed with bows, spears, clubs and throwing sticks; some carry a shaman''s charm.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.114-115');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'pygmy-shaman', 'Pygmy Shaman', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, mostly good or anarchist', '{"IQ":"3D6 min 12","ME":"3D6 min 14","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+2 min 16","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6+2"}', NULL, '20', NULL, '1D6X10+PE', NULL, 'Attributes are the pygmy''s (all 3D6, from the hunter entry); the +2 P.E. and +2 Spd bonuses are folded in, and the requirements (I.Q. 12, M.E. 14, P.E. 14) are floors before the bonus (so P.E. min 16). Hit points are not printed; the usual P.E. +1D6 per level applies. S.D.C. 20 is the racial bonus. P.P.E. is 1D6x10 plus the P.E. number, +2D4+2 per level after the first. No psionics or I.S.P. printed.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":1}', '+1 on saves vs every kind of magic, +4 to save vs Horror Factor. Attacks per melee come from Hand to Hand: Basic (Expert for one other skill).', 'Native tongue and Euro (+20%), one more language (+20%), basic math, Lore: Demons & Monsters, climb, land navigation, wilderness survival, identify plants, holistic medicine, palming, cook, dance, preserve food; W.P. Targeting and Blunt; four related skills plus more at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12; two secondary.', 'Knows the ley lines, nexuses and Millennium Trees of Central Africa and can draw on ley line energy.', 'Casts no spells. Makes talismans (one spell each at 4th level strength; spell P.P.E. +40 for single use, +200 for twice a day) and long-lasting protective charms (spell P.P.E. +100) in a 1D4 hour ritual, powered by his own P.P.E., a ley line, a nexus or a sacrifice. Carries 1D6+4 favourite items plus a dozen or two common ones to lend or trade.', NULL, '4 to 5 ft (1.2 to 1.5 m)', NULL, NULL, 'The Congo, as the shaman of a pygmy tribe', 'Tree people; reveres the agogwe', 'Supernatural beings and evil spirits', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C. Pygmy priests are mostly Millennium Druids and medicine men mostly Herbalists (Rifts England).', 'The tribal shaman of the pygmies, who cannot cast spells but pours mystic energy into protective charms and single-spell talismans that he lends to his people.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.115-116');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'agogwe', 'Agogwe', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Usually good or selfish, rarely evil', '{"IQ":"3D4","ME":"4D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"4D4","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+2","PB":"3D4","Spd":"5D6"}', NULL, '20', NULL, '2D6', 'ME+12', 'Hit points are not printed; the usual P.E. +1D6 per level would apply. S.D.C. 20 is the racial bonus. I.S.P. shown is the minor psionic (60%): M.E. +12, +1D6 per level. Major (37%): M.E. +20, +2D6 per level. Master (3%): M.E. +40, +3D6 per level.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":2}', '+2 to save vs all poisons and disease. Attacks per melee come from Hand to Hand: Basic (Expert for one other skill).', 'Native tongue 98%, Gobblely 75%; swim, climb, prowl, fish, track animals, land navigation (+15% jungle, +5% elsewhere), wilderness survival, identify plants, cook, preserve food, skin hides; W.P. Targeting, Blunt and one ancient W.P.; three related skills plus more at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12; three secondary at levels 3 and 9.', 'Nightvision 30 ft (9 m). Every agogwe is psychic. Fears magic and the supernatural and never uses magic items.', NULL, 'Roll percentile: 01-60 minor (three Sensitive powers); 61-97 major (Sense Evil, Sixth Sense and Mind Block plus six Healing and/or Sensitive powers); 98-00 master (four each of Super, Sensitive and Physical, one more from those every other level), often the tribe''s leader.', '5 ft to 5 ft 5 in (1.5 to 1.6 m)', NULL, NULL, 'Dense forest of the Congo, less often Uganda, Tanzania and Zambia, in nomadic clans of 4D4x10', 'Tree people; on good terms with the pygmies', NULL, 'R.C.C. with its own skills (Wilderness Man); takes no O.C.C.', 'Small, hairy, quick prehistoric humanoids long thought extinct, living as shy nomadic gatherers in the deep forest; all are psychic.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.117-118');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'tree-people', 'Tree People', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Usually good or selfish, rarely evil', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"4D6","PS":"3D4","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, '15', NULL, '3D6', NULL, 'Hit points are not printed; the usual P.E. +1D6 per level would apply. S.D.C. 15 is the racial bonus; the Running skill adds +1D6 S.D.C., +1 P.E. and +4D4 Spd. Spd is running or climbing; multiply by ten through the tree tops. The 10% who are master psionic healers have no I.S.P. printed.', NULL, NULL, '{"initiative":2}', '+1 attack per melee on top of Hand to Hand: Expert (hunter-warriors; females and non-hunters have Basic). +3 to save vs all poisons and disease. +3 to dodge during a running leap.', 'Native tongue 98%, Gobblely, Pygmy, Swahili and Euro 85%, one more language; acrobatics, gymnastics, climb, prowl, running, track animals, land navigation, wilderness survival, identify plants, cook; W.P. Targeting (60%) or bows (40%), Blunt and one ancient W.P.; three related skills plus more at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12; three secondary at levels 3 and 8.', 'Senses supernatural evil as a Dog Boy does. Nightvision 1000 ft (305 m) but only about 200 ft in bright sun; keen hearing and smell. Prehensile feet that grip weapons and tools. Glides on arm membranes: standing leap 30 ft, running leap up to 100 ft, glide speed about 11, up to half a mile from a great height.', NULL, 'Sense supernatural evil for all. 10% are master psionics with healing powers; the book gives no powers count or I.S.P.', '3 ft to 3 ft 4 in (0.9 to 1 m)', '30 to 50 lbs (13.6 to 22.6 kg)', NULL, 'Treetop villages in the Congo, less so Uganda and Kenya; tribes of 1D4x100 to 3D4x1000', 'Pygmies and agogwe', 'Slavers (minions of the Splugorth and Rama-Set), supernatural monsters, witches and evil magic', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C.', 'Tiny furry D-bees with huge bush-baby eyes and gliding membranes, curious, playful and light-fingered, who treat the Congo as their own and defend it fiercely.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.118-119');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'phoenixi-africa', 'Phoenixi', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; 40% unprincipled, 20% scrupulous, 40% other', '{"IQ":"2D6+8","ME":"4D6","MA":"4D6","PS":"4D6+2","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+12","PB":"4D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6X10', '3D4X100', '2D4X100', 'A mega-damage creature of magic; no hit points or S.D.C. printed. P.P.E. and I.S.P. each +10 per level after the first. While wreathed in flame it gains 20 more M.D.C. per level. Spd is running; flight is 3D4x10.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":"3-5","initiative":2}', 'NPCs average 3 to 5 attacks per melee, physical or psionic (Hand to Hand: Expert), or two by magic. +20% on coma/death rolls; +2 vs poisons, drugs and other foreign chemicals. Horror Factor +3 while aflame.', 'Basic and advanced math, astronomy, land navigation, navigation, wilderness survival, intelligence, Dragonese (read and speak), Gobblely; Hand to Hand: Expert; two ancient and one modern W.P.; two technical or science skills, two rogue or communications skills; plus five secondary and an extra Earth language.', 'Flies on flaming wings. Impervious to fire and heat, needs no air, hawk-like sight, nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees the invisible, heals ten times as fast as a human, resists drugs and disease, usually speaks by telepathy. Can burst into flame that burns only what it chooses (+2D6 M.D. to hand to hand, fire bolt). Once per 12 hours can instantly regenerate fully from as low as -30 M.D.C., and can go 1D6x10 days without food, water or sleep.', 'Every fire spell, along with Mystic Portal, Close Rift and Dimensional Portal.', 'Telepathy, Pyrokinesis and all Healing and Physical powers.', '10 to 14 ft (3 to 4.3 m)', '400 to 700 lbs (180 to 315 kg)', '900 years', 'Forests and wild places where they can fly; small groups in Africa, India, Asia and the Phoenix Empire; travels alone, in pairs or in groups of 1D4+2', 'Bennu and other champions of good, though most keep neutral', 'Good ones may oppose the Gods of Taut and evil; most stay overtly neutral', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C.', 'Tall crane-headed bird people with red and gold plumage and flaming wings, children of Bennu who roam the Megaverse as detached explorers; they never wear armor.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.60-61');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'ramen-africa', 'Ramen', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; 50% principled, 40% scrupulous, 10% other', '{"IQ":"3D6+3","ME":"5D6","MA":"4D6","PS":"6D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"4D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4X100', '1D6X10+40', '1D6X10+40', 'A supernatural mega-damage creature; no hit points or S.D.C. printed. P.P.E. +6 and I.S.P. +1D6+1 per level after the first. Supernatural P.S.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":"4-6","initiative":3}', 'Printed NPC average of four to six hand to hand attacks (martial arts and boxing), or two by magic. +1 on all saving throws. Half damage from psionic attacks; impervious to mind control.', 'Basic math, Dragonese (read and speak), Gobblely and ancient Egyptian; Hand to Hand: Martial Arts; climb, prowl, track, intelligence, wilderness survival, horsemanship; two physical skills; three ancient and three modern W.P.; two technical or communications skills; five secondary plus one Earth language.', 'Half damage from all psionic attacks, impervious to mind control, nightvision 70 ft (21 m), heals twice as fast as a human, resists disease. Domestic animals take to it at once (+20% to ride or handle); wild animals ignore it; can psionically make an animal flee or submit.', '40% are effectively Mystics but gain only four spells at first level and two per level after that.', 'Mind Block, Bio-Regeneration, Nightvision, Presence Sense, Empathy, Empathic Transmission and Psionic Empathy with Animals (range 10 ft per level, 5 I.S.P. to control).', '12 ft (3.6 m)', '750 to 900 lbs (337.5 to 405 kg)', '250 years', 'Forests and wilderness; tribes of 3D4x10 in Africa, Turkey, Afghanistan and India; a 57-strong renegade band serves Rama-Set in Egypt', 'Ra''s pantheon (the Egyptian Gods of Light) and other good champions', 'Supernatural monsters, demons and evil, above all the tautons; Anhur is opposed only reluctantly', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C.', 'Giant tan lion-headed knights sworn to Ra''s pantheon, noble and brave, with a deep bond to animals; about two in five have mystic magic.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.61-63');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'tauton', 'Tauton', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Mostly diabolic, miscreant or anarchist; an unprincipled or good tauton is an outcast', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"6D6+6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"2D4","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4X100', '1D4X100', NULL, 'A supernatural mega-damage being; no hit points or S.D.C. printed. P.P.E. +10 per level after the first. I.S.P. printed as None. Supernatural P.S. Many wear heavy 120 M.D.C. body armor. I.S.P.: none (printed as N/A or None).', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":"4-6","initiative":3}', 'Printed NPC average of four to six hand to hand attacks (martial arts and boxing) plus one for the tail, or two by magic. +1 on all saving throws, +2 more vs drugs; impervious to poison.', 'Basic math, Dragonese (read and speak), Gobblely and ancient Egyptian; Hand to Hand: Martial Arts; prowl, track humanoids, track animals, intelligence, wilderness survival; two wilderness, two espionage or rogue, three ancient and two modern W.P., two technical and two communications skills; five secondary plus one Earth language.', 'Nightvision 70 ft (21 m), sees the invisible, half damage from heat, fire and cold, can turn into a large venomous snake, swims 98%, holds breath 3D4 minutes, sees well in murky water, heals twice as fast as a human. Scorpion tail adds one melee attack.', 'Ley line magic: seven spells from levels 1-4, three more at level 2, then three from levels 1-9 at levels 4, 7, 9, 12 and 15.', NULL, '11 ft (3.35 m)', '600 to 900 lbs (270 to 405 kg)', '200 years', 'Deserts and forests near water; a few thousand serve Pharaoh Rama-Set, others roam Africa', 'The Egyptian dark gods and assorted villains, among them the Four Horsemen; sometimes the Worms of Taut', 'The ramen above all, plus the Gods of Light and every force for good; Sebek shuns them', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C.', 'Giant crocodile-headed humanoids with scorpion tails, discarded minions of Set''s pantheon grown bitter and cruel, obsessed with destroying the ramen.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.63-64');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO creatures (slug, name, category, system, playable, alignment, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, pools_note, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, size, weight, life_span, habitat, allies, enemies, occ_note, description, source_book) VALUES (
  'crocodillian', 'Crocodillian', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, mostly anarchist, unprincipled, miscreant or aberrant', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"2D4+28","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6X10', '2D4X10', '3D4X10', 'A supernatural mega-damage being; no hit points or S.D.C. printed. M.D.C. +10 per level; I.S.P. +1D6+1 per level. Spd is running and doubles when swimming. Supernatural P.S.', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', 'Three attacks at level one, +1 at levels 3, 5, 9, 12 and 15; no hand to hand skill. The +3 initiative and +2 strike, parry and dodge double in or under water. +3 to save vs Horror Factor. Dehydration after eight hours out of water: each day -50% Spd, -2 to combat and saves, -10% skills, cumulative; coma and death after six days.', 'Basic math, Dragonese and Euro (read and speak), Gobblely and ancient Egyptian; track animals, land navigation, water and underwater navigation, wilderness survival; two wilderness or rogue, three technical and three W.P.; six secondary plus two at levels 4 and 8. Natural swim 98%, climb 45%, prowl 30% (70% in water).', 'Nightvision 200 ft (61 m), sees the invisible, infrared sight in murky water, half damage and duration from heat, fire, cold, poison and drugs, tracks by blood scent 82%, holds breath 4D4 minutes, heals twice as fast (four times after six hours in water). Leaps 2D4 ft.', 'None; distrusts magic and avoids even magic weapons.', 'All psionic: 10% Mind Melters, 5% Mind Bleeders; the other 85% are master psionics with Hydrokinesis, P.P.E. Shield, Psionic Empathy with Reptiles, four Sensitive and two Healing powers, plus two Sensitive and one Healing at levels 5 and 10.', 'About 20 ft (6 m) long, 4 ft (1.2 m) tall on all fours, 11 ft (3.35 m) standing', '1000 to 2000 lbs (450 to 900 kg)', '300 years', 'Rivers, swamps and lakes away from cold climates, mostly in Africa and India, often among ordinary crocodiles', 'Sebek alone formally; likes crocodiles and humans', 'Dislikes the Gods of Darkness (Set and Anubis most), tautons and the meddling Gods of Light; opposes the Four Horsemen', 'R.C.C. with its own skills; takes no O.C.C.', 'Crocodile-like D-bees rescued from extinction by Sebek, whom they serve as spies and messengers; they move on all fours, love technology and shun magic.', 'Rifts World Book 4: Africa p.67-69');

